<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32441" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏlĕāgĭnĕus</span></b> ,
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏlĕāgĭnĭus</span></b> ,
		and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏlĕ-āgĭnus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		olea. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to the
				olive-tree</i> (for the class. olearius): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oleagineum seminarium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 48</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">radix,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 2, 31</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virgulae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep. Thras. 4, 1</span></i>
			: oleagineis coronis ministri triumphantium utebantur, quod
			Minerva dea belli esse putabatur, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				192</span></i> Müll.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Resembling an olive-tree</i> or <i>an
				olive</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitis oleaginia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 2, 27</span></i>
			 dub.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					14, 3, 4, § 38</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Olive-colored</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">berylli oleagini,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					37, 5, 20, § 77</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
